---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="what is the minimal fix" description="agents add guardrails they cannot see already exist. reduction is still a skill.">
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="font-mono text-xs text-faint mb-4">
      <a href="/writing" class="text-accent hover:underline">writing</a> <span class="text-faint">/</span> what-is-the-minimal-fix
    </div>

    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-normal animate-fade-up">what is the minimal fix</h1>

    <div class="essay mt-10 animate-fade-up delay-1">
      <p>one useful skill i picked up from the manual coding era is reduction.</p>
      <p>ai agents love to add guardrails inside the repo because they can’t see that the same guardrail already exists in another part of the system.</p>
      <p>then all the pieces come together and the user gets blocked twice from the same flow.</p>
      <hr class="my-12 border-border" />
      <p>so i keep spamming esc to stop the agent and ask: what is the minimal fix that can finish the job?</p>
      <p>most of the time the agent corrects itself mid-turn. minimal loc to get it done. no more spaghetti.</p>
      <hr class="my-12 border-border" />
      <p>software maintenance skill is still in trend i guess. not exactly the end of the software engineer era like the doomers say.</p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-spice">sometimes less is better.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-6 border-t border-border">
      <a href="/writing" class="text-accent hover:underline">← back to writing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .essay p {
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
